2026-09-25T20:10Z — design decisions (reported, not asked)
- Ledger writer placed in services/enrich/snapshots.py (the enrichment persistence module, already
  in the privacy allow-set) using jina.estimate_jina_search_cost; synthesize.py byte-untouched.
- The enrich JOB is created before the ledger row so the row joins the household (job_id not None);
  the reader joins through job, so a None-job row would be invisible to the cap.
- Only a Jina request that actually left the machine is charged (`jina.request_was_sent`):
  a missing-key refusal returns before the transport and records no cost row.
- Added a monthly-cap gate to api/v1/enrich.py mirroring run_ai_extraction's durable month check
  (the packet's success-delta demands the enrich trigger refuse on household spend at cap).
  No cap VALUE changed; the gate is inert while sg_monthly_cap is None (the live default).

